# Inventory IMPEX (inventory.xsd)

Before changing inventory XML builders, **read** `.cursor/references/sfcc-xsd/inventory.xsd`. Sequences are ordered. A valid element in the wrong place fails import (`cvc-complex-type.2.4.a`).

Namespace: `http://www.demandware.com/xml/impex/inventory/2007-05-31`. Root is `<inventory>` containing `<inventory-list>` children. Skip empty optional elements. Do not invent tags (`preorderable`, `backorderable` are **not** in this schema).

## Inventory list

`header` (required) → `records`

## Header (`complexType.Header`)

`list-id` is required.

`default-instock` (required boolean) → `description` → `use-bundle-inventory-only` → `on-order` (header boolean: whether this list tracks on-order) → `custom-attributes`

## Record (`complexType.InventoryRecord`)

`product-id` is required (max 100).

`allocation` (≥ 0) → `allocation-timestamp` (`xsd:dateTime`) → `perpetual` → `preorder-backorder-handling` (`none` | `preorder` | `backorder`) → `preorder-backorder-allocation` → `in-stock-date` (deprecated `xsd:date`) → **`in-stock-datetime`** (`xsd:dateTime`) → `ats` → `on-order` → `turnover` → `custom-attributes`

Do **not** emit `ats`, `on-order`, or `turnover` on import — they are calculated / read-only. Prefer `in-stock-datetime` over deprecated `in-stock-date`.

**Runtime maps** (Check Attributes `attrIdMap_inventory`): record custom fields are resolved at write time. `allocation` / `ATS` are OOTB (`ATS` is export-only — never emit). Other targets become `<custom-attribute>`.

Builders: `inventoryMigration/inventoryXmlBuilder.js`, `productMigration/inventoryXmlBuilder.js`.
